==Overview==
<tabber>
Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* Usable for PvP if used correctly.
* Able to evade ground based attacks.

|'''[Z] Plumage'''
* Helped users [[jump]] a little higher.
* Quick transform.

|'''[X] Wind Burst'''
* Slight knockback.

|'''[C] Bone Crusher'''
* Good stun.

|'''[V] Soaring Talon'''
* Good mobility.
* Moderate combo potential.

|'''[F] Flight'''
* Decent speed.
}}

|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* Required good aim for [[Blox Fruit]] mains because of the small hitbox.
* Very bad for grinding due to single target and knockback.
* Low damage.

|'''[Z] Plumage'''
* Boosts from this move were minimal and practically useless for high level players.

|'''[X] Wind Burst'''
* Easy to avoid.
* Bad range.

|'''[C] Bone Crusher'''
* Single-target.
* Bad range.
* The user could still take damage while stunning a target, making it ineffective for grinding.

|'''[V] Soaring Talon'''
* Easy to avoid.

|'''[F] Flight'''
* Relatively slow.
}}
</tabber>

==Trivia==
* Falcon was one of two [[Blox Fruits]] to have "Bird:" in their name, along [[Phoenix]].
* Falcon was the only {{Uncommon}} [[Beast]]-type fruit.
* Falcon was the cheapest [[Beast]] Blox Fruit in [[money]] and value.
* If the player used '''[Z] Plumage''' and switches to another [[Blox Fruit]], they would keep Falcon's wings, along with the buffs.
** The player would lose these wings when they died, switched teams, or left the game.
* Falcon was sometimes considered half-beast by the community, as it did not have a full [[transformation]].
** This was slightly justified, as it could see some use in most cases, though its moves were not very powerful by most measures.

